Firmware for the OpenCM9.04 board used to control the inspector
Makefile description:
Use "make" to build the project
Use "make flash" to flash the program to an OpenCM board -> the port can be changed in core/robotis-loader
If OpenCM9.04 does not download the program, connect the USB cable while holding down the “User Button”. Status LED will stay lit and the download will be initiated.
Use "make clean" to clean up project -> use make clean before commit with git!

Install ARM EABI compiler from code sourcery

#download
wget https://sourcery.mentor.com/sgpp/lite/arm/portal/package8736/public/arm-none-eabi/arm-2011.03-42-arm-none-eabi.bin

#Modify dash
sudo dpkg-reconfigure -plow dash 
#ANSWER WITH NO!

# Now bash is the default /bin/sh and not dash!
ls -lh /bin/sh

# Create the install dir.
mkdir -p  /home/feesma44884/Programme/arm-2011.03-42-arm-none-eabi

#Start installer
/bin/sh arm-2011.03-42-arm-none-eabi.bin

#Install options:
- minimal installation
- install dir (see above)
- No add to path!
- Don't create links

#Finished